     "title": "Jaguar offers a first look inside the all-electric Type 01",
     "url": "https://www.theverge.com/transportation/978793/jaguar-type-01-interior",
     "time": "08-12 21:48",
     "ts": 1786542528,
     "summary": "Jaguar's all-electric Type 01 comes with a very beige interior that divides the four seats with a \"spine\" that spans the length of the cabin. New photos shared ",
     "source": "The Verge Transport",
     "content": "Jaguar’s all-electric Type 01 comes with a very beige interior that divides the four seats with a “spine” that spans the length of the cabin. New photos shared by Jaguar show a low-slung driver’s seat, alongside a slim dashboard with a smartphone-style display in the center.\nJaguar offers a first look inside the all-electric Type 01\nJaguar’s upcoming EV has a minimalist cabin with a smartphone-style display.\nJaguar’s upcoming EV has a minimalist cabin with a smartphone-style display.\nThis vehicle doesn’t come with a traditional rear-view mirror, as Jaguar says you’ll find a “ClearSight Rear View Display” at the very bottom of the windshield, positioned at the “same height as the door mirrors, to help the driver focus.” There are also some “concealed compartments” and “hidden‑until‑needed technologies” according to Jaguar, though you can’t make any of that out in the photos.\nThe Type 01 is a follow-up to the polarizing Type 00 concept Jaguar first revealed in 2024, and is the first production vehicle built on Jaguar’s Electric Architecture. Jaguar will show off the Type 01 prototype under a camo wrap at Monterey Car Week before its official reveal on October 6th.",
     "_extract_method": "trafilatura",
