     "title": "EPO revokes Hanwha cell passivation patent",
     "url": "https://www.pv-tech.org/epo-revokes-hanwha-cell-passivation-patent/",
     "time": "08-13 19:13",
     "ts": 1786619602,
     "summary": "South Korean PV producer Hanwha Solutions, parent company of Q Cells, has had a long-contested passivation patent revoked in Europe.",
     "source": "PV Tech",
     "content": "South Korean PV producer Hanwha Solutions, parent company of Q Cells, has had a long-contested passivation patent revoked in Europe.\nThe Board of Appeal of the European Patent Office (EPO) last month revoked patent EP2220689, which covers solar cells with a surface passivating dielectric double layer, a technology that reduces recombination losses and boosts efficiency.\nTry Premium for just $1\n- Full premium access for the first month at only $1\n- Converts to an annual rate after 30 days unless cancelled\n- Cancel anytime during the trial period\nPremium Benefits\n- Expert industry analysis and interviews\n- Digital access to PV Tech Power journal\n- Exclusive event discounts\nOr get the full Premium subscription right away\nOr continue reading this article for free\nRevocation of the patent followed oral hearings in July. Although a final document on the ruling has not yet been published, specialist patent media outlet Juve Patent reported that the decision was due to the lack of an inventive step.\nAt the centre of the dispute was a passivation technology developed by Qcells and commercialised as its proprietary Q.ANTUM technology, which Hanwha said plays a role in improving the efficiency and performance of silicon-based solar cells.\nThe patent had been the subject of legal wrangling for over a decade across numerous jurisdictions, with leading PV manufacturers including LONGi, REC Solar, Trina Solar and Jinko Solar involved in litigation.\nIn 2020, a German court ruled in favour of Hanwha in its dispute with Jinko, LONGi and REC. In 2023, Hanwa and Trina reached a patent licensing and transfer agreement following a court ruling the previous year against Trina’s German subsidiary over the contested patent. REC Solar was reportedly the final appellant remaining in the case.\nHanwha had separately asserted its rights to the patent in the US and Australia, where EP689 has parallel designations, Juve Patent reported.\nPV Tech has contacted Hanwha for comment.\nThe dispute is one of many intellectual property battles that have convulsed the global PV manufacturing business in recent years as manufacturers seek strategic advantage over their competitors through so-called ‘lawfare’.",
     "_extract_method": "trafilatura",
     "zh": "欧洲专利局撤销韩华Q Cells钝化专利",
     "content_zh": "韩国光伏企业韩华解决方案（Q Cells母公司）在欧争议多年的钝化专利被撤销。欧洲专利局（EPO）上诉委员会上月撤销EP2220689号专利，该专利覆盖带表面钝化介质双层的太阳能电池技术，可减少复合损耗、提升效率。专利撤销源于7月的口头听证会，据专业专利媒体Juve Patent报道，撤销原因是该专利缺乏创造性。争议核心是Q Cells开发并作为 proprietary Q.ANTUM技术商业化的钝化技术，韩华称该技术对提升效率有重要作用。"
